Description: Recognize Mesa virgl in Firefox's WebGL renderer sanitizer
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: Asterinas development team

The QEMU DRM guest exposes a truthful Mesa renderer string beginning with
"virgl". ESR 140 currently maps that string to Generic Renderer, which makes
the WebGL gate fail even when GBM/EGL and glxtest both identify virgl. Keep the
strict runtime renderer check and teach the sanitizer this renderer family. The
regression test uses the same prefix and expected public label.

--- a/dom/canvas/SanitizeRenderer.cpp
+++ b/dom/canvas/SanitizeRenderer.cpp
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 static std::optional<std::string> ChooseDeviceReplacement(
     const std::string& str) {
   if (str.find("llvmpipe") == 0) return "llvmpipe";
+  if (str.find("virgl") == 0) return "virgl";
   if (str.find("Apple") == 0) return "Apple M1";
 
   std::smatch m;
--- a/dom/canvas/gtest/TestSanitizeRenderer.cpp
+++ b/dom/canvas/gtest/TestSanitizeRenderer.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,14 @@
 std::string SanitizeRenderer(const std::string&);
 }  // namespace mozilla::webgl
 
+TEST(SanitizeRenderer, TestLinuxVirgl)
+{
+  const std::string renderer("virgl (Mesa 25.0.7-2+deb13u1)");
+  const std::string expectation("virgl, or similar");
+  const auto sanitized = mozilla::webgl::SanitizeRenderer(renderer);
+  EXPECT_EQ(sanitized, expectation);
+}
